     to it specifies the desired set of features to be enabled in the API and
     the kernel.  The return value in _v is the actual (sub)set of features
     that were enabled in the kernel.  To obtain later the same set of fea‐
     tures that were enabled, use:

           getsockopt(sock, IPPROTO_IP, MRT_API_CONFIG, &v, sizeof(v));

     The set of enabled features is global.  In other words,
     sseettssoocckkoopptt(_M_R_T___A_P_I___C_O_N_F_I_G) should be called right after
     sseettssoocckkoopptt(_M_R_T___I_N_I_T).

